## Snap Shot targeting (C32, LoS math superseded 2026-08-03 by C35/C39)

Snap resolves at its **completion** second and wounds only near the **aimed point** (free-aim, not a tile — C39) with clear LoS — it does not sweep the line. Lanes are Hold Angle's job. LoS was integer Bresenham on tiles; is now continuous segment-vs-obstacle intersection (C35/C39) — the "never a physics raycast" rule carries over unchanged, only the math changed from grid to continuous.

## Move authoring (C21, amended 2026-08-03; coordinate type superseded same day by C35/C39)

**Supersedes the original allot-seconds-to-derive-stance model.** Player taps waypoints (each tap adds one; consecutive waypoints auto-connect via the shortest legal route — now continuous/Euclidean, not grid-orthogonal, per C35/C39 — player controls route shape, not a single system shortest-path). **Revisiting/crossing a previously-tapped point is legal** — no duplicate-tile guard. Player picks Sprint/Walk/Crawl **directly**, no time-allotment slider. Cost (`distance × BaseSecondsPerTile × StanceMult`, distance now Euclidean not tile-count) is computed and deducted automatically the instant the Move is scheduled; HUD shows running used/budget, never a pre-commit value. Matches how Shoot already worked (pick Snap/Hold, cost follows).

## Match pool / Time Card (C33)

One **shared** match Time Resource pool (demo **900s**). Each round one side plays a **Time Card** committing **N** seconds; round 1 = Attacker, then **alternates**. Both sides Program simultaneously inside **N**. **N spent in full** (unused burned). Positions + wounds **carry** across rounds. Match ends on Dead or when pool cannot fund another MinRound. Time Card ≠ gear card. **Numerics:** MinRoundSeconds = 30s (GDD §6); Allot UI presets 30s/60s/120s/ALL IN (remaining) + custom slider clamped to `[MinRoundSeconds, Remaining]`.

